      "extract": "WHO/POLIO/23.02 Poliovirus containment GUIDANCE TO MINIMIZE RISKS FOR FACILITIES COLLECTING, HANDLING OR STORING MATERIALS POTENTIALLY INFECTIOUS FOR POLIOVIRUSES, SECOND EDITION WEB ANNEX A COUNTRY- AND AREA-SPECIFIC POLIOVIRUS DATA, APRIL 2023 UPDATE Poliovirus containment: guidance to minimize risks for facilities collecting, handling or storing materials potentially infectious for polioviruses, second edition.",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-000-table-a21-country--and-area-specific-poliovirus",
      "number": null,
      "title": "Table A2.1. Country- and area-specific poliovirus circulation data, April 2023 update",
      "level": 2,
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 29,
      "labelStart": "4",
      "labelEnd": null,
      "words": 10132,
      "summary": {
        "text": "Table A2.1 lists, country by country from Afghanistan onwards, the periods when materials collected there may be potentially infectious for wild or circulating vaccine-derived polioviruses of types 1, 2 and 3. A further column gives the periods when samples may contain type 2 oral polio vaccine or Sabin2-related virus, which must be mitigated, while types 2 and 3 must be contained now. Footnotes explain special cases and territories listed under other countries. The table is followed by a long reference list of surveillance reports and studies on poliovirus circulation.",
        "status": "draft"
      },
